From 1833276ee5549176d5db286146eadede1a44f16d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:19:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: the real pad as a seat's input, all-AI tests without
 the AI crash, test switches

- SRNP_INPUT=manette: the machine's real pad, read from the emulated controller of a port the game
  does not see (GCPad4 by default, SRNP_MANETTE_PORT; its SI device set to None), clamped as the
  SDK's PADClamp, is sent to the relay as the seat's input. The game only gets it back through the
  relay, on every machine at once (no local pause from a local Start).
- SRNP_TOUS_CPU=1 now flags the players' racers CPU at setup (+0xBD = 1, the AI's data is made)
  but leaves them driven as humans (+0xBC = 0); the AI takes them at the start.
  SRNP_TOUS_CPU=ancien keeps the old way.
- A racer given to the AI points to the game's own controller structure again, as the game's CPUs.
- SRNP_IA_JOUEURS=<n>: only seats 0 to n-1 are simulated players. SRNP_HUMAINS=<hex mask>: which
  racers get the humans' flag at the start (tests of the missing scenery: it goes as soon as racer
  5 is a human, whatever its character; see AllCpuMode).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
