+// SRNP_TOUS_CPU=1 (tests: the AI drives every racer, the menu's players' too): the players' racers
+// get the CPUs' flag when the race is set up (+0xBD = 1: the game then makes their AI's data) but stay
+// driven as humans (+0xBC = 0); the AI takes them at the start. With +0xBD = 0 at setup, the AI reads
+// data the game did not make and crashes (0x80472A30). SRNP_TOUS_CPU=ancien: both bytes at 1 at setup.
+// Measured 2026-11-25, the scenery (roads, tubes, buildings missing after ~14"): it does not depend on
+// these bytes at setup but on the humans' flag during the race. Missing as soon as racer 5 is a human
+// (+0xBD = 0), whatever its character (SRNP_HUMAINS=21: racers 0 and 5 only, Ulala or Knuckles), and
+// with no human at all; whole with racers 6 or 7 human (41, 81), or any humans among racers 0-4. For
+// a human racer 4 the game sets up a lot of the DOL's BSS (0x801B7380, 0x801D76B0...), for racer 5
+// nothing of it. Not understood yet.
+int AllCpuMode()
+{
+  static const int mode = [] {
+    const char* v = std::getenv("SRNP_TOUS_CPU");
+    if (!v)
+      return 0;
+    const std::string_view m(v);
+    return m == "1" ? 1 : m == "ancien" ? 2 : 0;
+  }();
+  return mode;
+}
+
